      "writtenOn": "2024-07-19T02:14:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding a field to a trace event should never cause issues. The binary location of the fields must be found via the `format` files, which I believe Perfetto uses.\n```\n# cat /sys/kernel/tracing/events/block/block_rq_requeue/format \nname: block_rq_requeue\nID: 1420\nformat:\n\tfield:unsigned short common_type;\toffset:0;\tsize:2;\tsigned:0;\n\tfield:unsigned char common_flags;\toffset:2;\tsize:1;\tsigned:0;\n\tfield:unsigned char common_preempt_count;\toffset:3;\tsize:1;\tsigned:0;\n\tfield:int common_pid;\toffset:4;\tsize:4;\tsigned:1;\n\n\tfield:dev_t dev;\toffset:8;\tsize:4;\tsigned:0;\n\tfield:sector_t sector;\toffset:16;\tsize:8;\tsigned:0;\n\tfield:unsigned int nr_sector;\toffset:24;\tsize:4;\tsigned:0;\n\tfield:char rwbs[8];\toffset:28;\tsize:8;\tsigned:0;\n\tfield:__data_loc char[] cmd;\toffset:36;\tsize:4;\tsigned:0;\n```",
      "revId": "ca309998b54972f4fb2832e7993278df44e2077f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
